  "excerpt": "Fatteh is a Levantine layered dish of toasted or fried flatbread pieces soaked under a warm chickpea broth, then covered with garlicky yoghurt and pine nuts. Eaten warm, it is at once crisp and tart, and one of the most satisfying dishes in the Levantine kitchen.",
