  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Fatteh is a dish of contrasts. Crisp toasted bread underneath. Warm, garlicky yoghurt on top. Soft chickpeas in between, soaked in a little of their own warm liquid. The timing matters: assemble it at the last moment so the bread retains some of its crunch at the edges."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The yoghurt sauce is sharp and garlicky. Pine nuts and a drizzle of olive oil go over the top. A pinch of paprika gives a little colour. Eaten with a spoon, each bite gets all the layers at once."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Toasting the bread in the oven rather than frying gives a slightly lighter result. Frying in oil gives a richer, crispier result. Both work."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
